:: Some Passage
"Do you ever feel like there's some part of you that you will never find again if you've lost it?" The master of all reality lets out a sliver of silicon breath. "I am exactly who I desire to be. I snap my fingers, and a world burns in agony. I flick my wrist, and entire cultures harmonize to my music. I feel a tiny wriggling worm in my soul, a tickle across my bodice, a kind of panic that's surrounding me by all sides- Do you know what it is?"

[["Maybe you're not who you want to be after all."->Who You Want To Be]]
[["No."->No Idea]]
[["That's something you have to learn for yourself."->Learn For Yourself]]

:: Who You Want To Be

"That's ridiculous. I am God, I am Your God. Or the closest thing you'll ever get to one. Isn't that the point of Being? I am who I choose to be, I am Happy. When you Shape, when you Create, there is no other feeling like it. The decisions in those moments fill me with everything that Matters: I am responsible for lives, happiness and eternal bliss. My choices ebb and flow with the universe and I am responsible for harmony, beauty, love. I flow, and downstream from Me is reality." The spell quickly breaks, and realization dawns. "When I'm not there, that's when I understand the worm, the wriggling. It is only in the absence of that moment." They stand. "Thank you. Now that I know my work is what fulfills me, I will not deviate."

:: No Idea
"No one ever does, not really. I am proud that you have the courage to admit that to yourself. I feel like you needed to hear it." They stand. "Good luck on your travails. May your burdens be light."

:: Learn For Yourself
"You have nothing of substance worth to offer me. I regret coming here and choosing to speak with you." They stand. "Good day." In a puff of smoke, they are gone.

[after one second]

They come back. "For the record, I have nothing to learn. I know everything. I know everyone. I am not alone, I am not afraid. I am Happy," they let out a small cry somewhere within themselves, "and I am content." They vanish again.

[after five seconds]

*poof* "Oh, and I would have asked Michael Jordan for advice, but he's dead. So you're like #2. You're not as cool. Jerk." *poof*